# Package manager: Yarn only

Use **Yarn** for installs, adds, removes, and script execution in this project. Do not use npm or npx unless a tool has no Yarn equivalent and you state why.

## Commands

| Instead of | Use |
|---|---|
| `npm install` / `npm ci` | `yarn` / `yarn install` |
| `npm install <pkg>` | `yarn add <pkg>` |
| `npm install -D <pkg>` | `yarn add -D <pkg>` |
| `npm uninstall <pkg>` | `yarn remove <pkg>` |
| `npm run <script>` | `yarn <script>` |
| `npx <pkg>` | `yarn dlx <pkg>` |
| `npx create-<tool>` | `yarn create <tool>` or `yarn dlx create-<tool>` |

## Scaffolding

When a CLI offers a package-manager flag (e.g. `create-medusa-app`), pass `--use-yarn`.

## Lockfiles

- Prefer and commit `yarn.lock` (storefront root and `commerce/`).
- Do not create or commit `package-lock.json`.
- Do not run `npm install` in a Yarn project if it would regenerate a lockfile conflict.
